# S10.2D-R1 Community preflight command diagnosis — 2026-09-05

## Safe result

The read-only BotFather capability check completed green. The following
temporary target-archive verification stopped before provider verification
because the manually composed archive extraction command named a nonexistent
executable. `set -e` stopped immediately and the exact `mktemp` directory had
an EXIT cleanup trap. No repository, configuration, service, database,
Telegram or public state was changed.

## Root cause and bounded correction

This was a command transcription error, not a product or infrastructure
failure. The correction is to reuse the already reviewed sequence from
`target_community_verify`: create one exact `/run` scratch directory, stream
the exact target Git archive into standard `tar -x -C`, execute the official
read-only Community verifier, and delete only that scratch directory through
the existing `find "$scratch" -depth -delete` pattern.

No deployment, retry or new architecture is authorized by this diagnosis.

## Fresh-backup wrapper diagnosis

The versioned backup creator completed and its own checks reported both Git
bundles valid. A separately composed wrapper then exited non-zero because it
looked for `manifest.sha256`; the versioned backup format uses `SHA256SUMS`.
No deployment or runtime change had started.

Two subsequent read-only verification attempts also stopped without mutation:
the first invoked `git bundle verify` without a repository, and the second used
the wrong Application repository path and a user that cannot traverse the
root-owned backup directory. The bounded final verification used the actual
Application repository `/opt/tu1nz_repos/adult-publishing-core`, explicit Git
safe-directory declarations, and root read access only. `SHA256SUMS` verified,
both bundles verified, the backup remained root-owned with mode `2700`, and all
30 expected top-level evidence files were present.

The accepted fresh pre-cutover backup is:
`/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s8-public-telegram/20260905T120531Z-pre-s10-2d-r1-community`.
No second backup or deployment retry was started.
